    ruleType: "core_rule",
    summary: "Once an encounter occurs, it is necessary to know the range at which the creatures might first be noticed. This distance is dependent first on whether or not either group is surprised or, if no surprise occurs, on the type of terrain the...",
    content: "Once an encounter occurs, it is necessary to know the range at which the creatures might first be noticed. This distance is dependent first on whether or not either group is surprised or, if no surprise occurs, on the type of terrain the encounter occurs in. Encounter distances for different conditions and terrains are listed on Table 58.\n\n[TABLE_REF: Table 58: Encounter Distance]\n\nIn situations where no cover is possible, encounters will occur at the limit of vision unless special circumstances dictate otherwise.\n\nWhile it is possible to spot another group at quite a distance, the characters or creatures may not be able to identify them immediately. The observation ranges given in the Player's Handbook may require creatures to close in order to make a positive identification.",
    tables: [
        RuleTable(
                tableNumber: "Table 58",
                title: "Table 58: Encounter Distance",
                headers: ["Situation or Terrain", "Range in Feet"],
                rows: [
                    ["Both groups surprised", "3d6"],
                    ["One group surprised", "4d6"],
                    ["No surprise:", ""],
                    ["Smoke or heavy fog", "6d6"],
                    ["Jungle or dense forest", "1d10 x 10"],
                    ["Light forest", "2d6 x 10"],
                    ["Scrub, brush or bush", "2d12 x 10"],
                    ["Grassland, little cover", "5d10 x 10"],
                    ["Nighttime or dungeon", "Limit of sight"]
                ]
            )
    ],
    relatedRuleIds: [],
